// Local.xcconfig.example
//
// Template for developer-local build settings. DO NOT commit a real Local.xcconfig.
// Purpose:
// - Provide a safe example showing how to supply ALICE_API_BASE_URL to the app
// - Demonstrate preserving Flutter's generated DART_DEFINES via $(inherited)
//
// Usage (developer machine):
// 1. Copy this file to Local.xcconfig in the same directory.
//    Example: cp Local.xcconfig.example Local.xcconfig
// 2. Base64-encode the full ALICE_API_BASE_URL=<URL> string.
// 3. Replace the placeholder in DART_DEFINES with the Base64 result.
// 4. Ensure Local.xcconfig is ignored by git.
// 5. Build/run using the Debug configuration.
//
// Notes / safety:
// - The value for ALICE_API_BASE_URL should be an absolute URL (scheme://host[:port]).
// - For local HTTP development use only: http://127.0.0.1:PORT
// - For remote development / staging use HTTPS (https://example.com).
// - Do NOT include user credentials, tokens, production secrets, or real network addresses.
// - Do not include Generated.xcconfig here; Debug.xcconfig already loads it.
// - Keep the DART_DEFINES value as a comma-delimited list of Base64-encoded define values.
// - This file intentionally contains only placeholders and instructions.

// Keep Flutter's generated DART_DEFINES by including $(inherited).
// The example format uses a Base64-encoded define value, not a raw URL.
// For local use, create a Local.xcconfig with the same pattern.
DART_DEFINES=$(inherited),<BASE64_ENCODED_ALICE_API_BASE_URL_DEFINE>
